WEBVTT

00:00:00.730 --> 00:00:03.600
I'm gonna be the first-star idol one day!

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:07.820
Nijino Yume's about to start her Aikatsu!

00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:16.370
Hi, Mister Moroboshi. {we usually do this way}

00:00:16.370 --> 00:00:19.330
It's been far too long. How have you been?

00:00:19.950 --> 00:00:24.080
Very good. Why the sudden call?

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:28.920
I heard about your performance in Japan this Saturday.

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:31.840
Thus, I have a bit of a favor to ask.

00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:46.060
I can't wait for Hime-senpai's concert!

00:00:46.060 --> 00:00:48.110
Yeah, the anticipation is killing me.

00:00:48.110 --> 00:00:50.980
I wish it could just be Saturday already.

00:00:50.980 --> 00:00:52.610
Good morning.

00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:55.360
Anna-sensei, good morning.

00:00:55.360 --> 00:00:56.860
Good morning.

00:00:56.860 --> 00:00:59.870
Nijino, head on over to the Headmaster's office.

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:04.000
He's got something to tell you.

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:07.000
Something to tell me?

00:01:08.630 --> 00:01:12.550
What could it be? Am I in trouble?

00:01:15.170 --> 00:01:16.380
Enter.

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:19.640
E-Excuse me.

00:01:24.890 --> 00:01:29.400
Nijino Yume. You are here for one reason and one reason only.

00:01:30.020 --> 00:01:32.150
I have a request.

00:01:32.150 --> 00:01:34.400
H-How can I help you?

00:01:34.780 --> 00:01:39.660
Are you aware that Shiratori Hime is planned to perform in the academy's Grand Hall?

00:01:39.660 --> 00:01:40.780
Of course!

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:45.660
I already got tickets for it! I'm really excited!{do students have to pay?}{good point?}

00:01:45.660 --> 00:01:47.460
The concert is cancelled.

00:01:48.710 --> 00:01:52.050
I was thinking of having you be her replacement.

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:55.050
You want me to perform?

00:01:55.050 --> 00:01:58.800
Yes, in Nijino Yume's First Solo Live.

00:03:40.360 --> 00:03:46.830
And that's why Nijino Yume will be taking Shiratori Hime's place for the concert!

00:03:49.910 --> 00:03:52.580
Wait, why Nijino-san?

00:03:52.920 --> 00:03:57.630
Shiratori was unexpectedly called to perform in Merlion Carey's Japan show. {I'm assuming this is Mariah Carey, a quick wiki shows she's beloved in japan}

00:03:57.630 --> 00:04:00.210
Fortune has smiled upon Nijino.

00:04:00.590 --> 00:04:02.340
That gets me going.

00:04:02.340 --> 00:04:05.600
Nijino, stand up and say a few words. Come on!

00:04:05.600 --> 00:04:07.350
O-Okay!

00:04:07.350 --> 00:04:11.270
Um, I'm nervous about it being my first solo live,

00:04:11.270 --> 00:04:14.850
but I'll do my very best to make it a successful concert.

00:04:16.860 --> 00:04:19.860
I'll be giving Nijino personal lessons.

00:04:19.860 --> 00:04:24.410
Everyone else in Song Class, you'll be helping out with Shiratori's concert!

00:04:24.410 --> 00:04:25.320
Yes! {this one girl jumped the gun and messed up the timing}

00:04:27.160 --> 00:04:30.490
It's crazy, am I finally in the spotlight?

00:04:30.490 --> 00:04:35.630
You sure are. You're the first one in our year to hold a concert in the Grand Hall.

00:04:35.630 --> 00:04:38.630
But why did the Headmaster pick you?

00:04:43.050 --> 00:04:46.140
He must have realized my greatness!

00:04:46.470 --> 00:04:48.180
That must be it.

00:04:48.180 --> 00:04:49.510
Yeah!

00:04:50.260 --> 00:04:52.140
Yume, are you okay?

00:04:52.140 --> 00:04:54.140
Huh? What do you mean?

00:04:54.600 --> 00:04:57.520
That was supposed to be Hime-senpai's stage.

00:04:57.860 --> 00:04:59.270
Yep!

00:04:59.270 --> 00:05:01.190
Which obviously means...

00:05:03.690 --> 00:05:04.650
Yume-chan!

00:05:04.650 --> 00:05:07.410
Yume-chan, I'm sure you can handle this.

00:05:07.700 --> 00:05:08.570
I will!

00:05:12.910 --> 00:05:16.620
Everyone, thank you!

00:05:17.880 --> 00:05:20.800
I'm so pumped up, I can't contain my excitement!

00:05:20.800 --> 00:05:25.380
All right, then. If you're this determined, I'll be behind you all the way.

00:05:25.380 --> 00:05:26.430
Me too.

00:05:26.430 --> 00:05:28.010
Thanks!

00:05:28.010 --> 00:05:31.930
And because it's so important, I was thinking about using this.

00:05:31.930 --> 00:05:35.690
Oh, the Glitter you got from your last performance.

00:05:36.020 --> 00:05:38.900
Yeah, a first live is a special moment.

00:05:38.900 --> 00:05:41.190
I've gotta pull out all the stops for my dress.

00:05:42.860 --> 00:05:44.690
Congratulations.

00:05:45.110 --> 00:05:49.950
Not everyone can get a Grade-Up Glitter this quickly.{I can't tell if Grade-Up Glitter looks better (or Grade Up Glitter}

00:05:49.950 --> 00:05:53.290
We're not exactly sure how to use it, though.

00:05:53.290 --> 00:05:54.950
Could you help us?

00:05:55.290 --> 00:05:56.580
Very well.

00:05:56.580 --> 00:05:59.540
Yuri-chan's Dress Make Seminar!

00:06:00.500 --> 00:06:05.210
By using Grade-Up Glitter, you'll be able to create Rare Dresses.{I feel like maybe "dress" should've been capitalized from the start. Are we allowed to begin now?}{okay, only in conjunction with other words}

00:06:05.210 --> 00:06:06.590
Rare Dresses?

00:06:06.590 --> 00:06:11.470
It's quite simple to do. First you place one of your Normal Dresses here. {so about this capitalization...}

00:06:12.560 --> 00:06:16.560
And when you overlay your Grade-Up Glitter...

00:06:17.520 --> 00:06:19.560
There's your Rare Dress!

00:06:20.600 --> 00:06:23.190
Well? Isn't it easy?

00:06:23.190 --> 00:06:24.190
Yes.

00:06:24.190 --> 00:06:25.990
Good luck then.

00:06:35.330 --> 00:06:37.660
My very first Rare Dress!

00:06:37.660 --> 00:06:40.670
The heart ribbon looks perfect for you.

00:06:40.670 --> 00:06:43.750
It's My Little Heart, same as Hime-senpai.

00:06:44.380 --> 00:06:48.760
Now to train myself to the same level as this Citrus Tea Time Coord.

00:06:49.720 --> 00:06:51.010
I'm back.

00:06:54.510 --> 00:06:57.640
Yume-chan, how's your practice coming along?

00:06:58.060 --> 00:07:00.140
Great! Look at this, Koharu-chan.

00:07:00.140 --> 00:07:02.400
Wait, isn't that song...

00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:04.440
Exactly! You remember it?

00:07:04.440 --> 00:07:07.280
It's from the concert we went to before we came to Four Star Academy.

00:07:07.650 --> 00:07:11.240
Hime-senpai sang this song there!

00:07:12.280 --> 00:07:16.200
I spoke with Anna-sensei about it and we decided to go ahead with this song.

00:07:16.200 --> 00:07:21.000
Yume-chan, you keep on getting closer to your dream of joining S4.

00:07:21.000 --> 00:07:22.710
Y-You think so?

00:07:22.710 --> 00:07:24.210
Absolutely!

00:07:26.920 --> 00:07:31.220
Oh, yeah! I should invite Mom and Dad to the concert!

00:07:32.640 --> 00:07:35.050
Headmaster, what are your intentions?

00:07:35.720 --> 00:07:37.930
Forcing a solo live onto her is...

00:07:37.930 --> 00:07:40.180
Too much responsibility?

00:07:42.310 --> 00:07:45.190
What do you think of Nijino Yume?

00:07:46.820 --> 00:07:48.690
I sense potential.

00:07:48.690 --> 00:07:51.240
That's just the way you would phrase it.

00:07:52.700 --> 00:07:57.200
If Yume-chan were to fail to complete her performance...

00:07:57.490 --> 00:08:02.420
Then I will have no choice but to remove her from Four Star Academy.

00:08:05.420 --> 00:08:09.960
Let's see, tickets... there's Mom and Dad.

00:08:10.340 --> 00:08:14.970
And then Koharu-chan and Rola... I wonder if I can reserve more.

00:08:16.930 --> 00:08:18.140
All full?!

00:08:21.850 --> 00:08:22.890
Huh?

00:08:22.890 --> 00:08:23.850
Hello!

00:08:23.850 --> 00:08:26.230
Good morning.

00:08:26.900 --> 00:08:28.730
Sensei, look at this!

00:08:29.360 --> 00:08:31.360
S-See?

00:08:32.950 --> 00:08:35.740
So no tickets have been sold at all.

00:08:37.320 --> 00:08:41.160
What do I do? Nobody is going to come...

00:08:41.160 --> 00:08:42.500
Go out and peddle.

00:08:43.710 --> 00:08:46.500
Don't you want everyone to watch you?

00:08:46.500 --> 00:08:49.880
Then you've got no choice but to sell those tickets yourself!

00:08:49.880 --> 00:08:51.670
Go, right now!

00:08:51.670 --> 00:08:52.970
O-Okay!

00:08:55.090 --> 00:09:00.640
<i>Headmaster, why did you choose Nijino if you knew this would happen?</i>

00:09:05.810 --> 00:09:07.900
Easier said than done.

00:09:07.900 --> 00:09:10.900
Can I really sell all these?

00:09:10.900 --> 00:09:13.570
Hey, it's Nijino Mame!

00:09:13.570 --> 00:09:14.900
It's Yume!

00:09:15.280 --> 00:09:16.910
So it was.

00:09:16.910 --> 00:09:20.660
It's nice to see you again, Yamaguchi-san. What are you doing here?

00:09:20.660 --> 00:09:23.790
We're recording at a studio nearby.

00:09:24.580 --> 00:09:28.960
Are you interested in coming to see my first solo live this Saturday?

00:09:28.960 --> 00:09:32.050
Sorry, we're going to be working on set that day.

00:09:32.340 --> 00:09:34.260
I see.

00:09:34.260 --> 00:09:36.260
Good luck with your recording.

00:09:38.590 --> 00:09:39.680
Director Okamoto.

00:09:40.220 --> 00:09:42.560
I'll be holding my first solo live soon...

00:09:42.560 --> 00:09:45.560
I have a filming that day.

00:09:45.560 --> 00:09:47.350
I see...

00:09:49.020 --> 00:09:53.820
Hello, my name is Nijino Yume. 
Is President Koumoto available?

00:09:53.820 --> 00:09:57.200
Very soon I'll be holding my first solo live—

00:09:56.360 --> 00:09:57.200
Sorry!

00:09:57.200 --> 00:10:00.160
I'm on vacation in Hawaii right now.

00:10:07.670 --> 00:10:08.960
I'm not finished!

00:10:11.670 --> 00:10:13.590
You're studying for exams?

00:10:13.590 --> 00:10:15.340
A TV show you don't want to miss?

00:10:16.380 --> 00:10:18.090
You'll go if you can?

00:10:18.090 --> 00:10:21.600
That definitely means you're not coming...

00:10:23.100 --> 00:10:24.930
Not a one...

00:10:25.430 --> 00:10:28.100
Stop, no more negativity!

00:10:28.600 --> 00:10:30.230
Attention!

00:10:30.560 --> 00:10:33.900
If you buy a ticket now, I'll throw in the second for free!

00:10:33.900 --> 00:10:36.280
And it's half-off! {oh, this is the bookstore from ep 6}

00:10:36.280 --> 00:10:39.150
Hey there, how would you like to buy a ticket?

00:10:39.780 --> 00:10:42.240
What is she doing?

00:10:43.620 --> 00:10:46.000
I couldn't make a single sale.

00:10:46.370 --> 00:10:51.210
Hey, did you hear? It doesn't look like 
anybody's going to Nijino-san's concert.

00:10:51.210 --> 00:10:54.250
You can't blame her. She doesn't have any fans yet.

00:10:54.250 --> 00:10:56.800
Why do you think they picked her?

00:10:56.800 --> 00:11:00.260
No idea, but it'd be hard for any of us first-years.

00:11:00.260 --> 00:11:02.010
Yume!

00:11:03.300 --> 00:11:05.310
I sold three tickets!

00:11:05.310 --> 00:11:06.520
Really?

00:11:06.520 --> 00:11:10.230
Yeah! Some of my fans said they could make it.

00:11:11.400 --> 00:11:13.690
I see. Thanks.

00:11:13.690 --> 00:11:14.520
Yume?

00:11:14.520 --> 00:11:18.280
O-Oh yeah, I need to head to my lesson.

00:11:18.280 --> 00:11:19.280
Yume!

00:11:27.620 --> 00:11:31.420
Who am I singing for?

00:11:42.510 --> 00:11:45.550
No, no! Once more, from the top.

00:11:45.550 --> 00:11:48.310
Wrong! Start over.

00:11:48.310 --> 00:11:51.440
That's not how it goes. Don't keep making the same mistakes!

00:11:51.440 --> 00:11:55.940
Solo lives require lots of stamina!
You can't get tired that quickly!

00:11:56.820 --> 00:12:00.070
<i>This is bad! I can't concentrate at all!</i>

00:12:03.240 --> 00:12:05.570
Why was it canceled?

00:12:05.570 --> 00:12:06.490
Tell us!

00:12:06.490 --> 00:12:09.200
I wanted to see you sing, Hime-senpai.

00:12:09.200 --> 00:12:15.210
I'm sorry. I promise to make up for it soon, so please wait until then.

00:12:17.340 --> 00:12:21.420
<i>Everyone was looking forward to Hime-senpai's concert.</i>

00:12:21.420 --> 00:12:23.470
<i>But nobody cares about mine...</i>

00:12:24.720 --> 00:12:25.890
<i>Yume-chan...</i>

00:12:37.480 --> 00:12:39.940
No! Isn't anybody here?

00:12:39.940 --> 00:12:41.740
Hey, someone!

00:12:46.370 --> 00:12:47.280
Yume.

00:12:48.410 --> 00:12:53.080
I finally understand what you meant, Rola.

00:12:53.910 --> 00:12:56.790
That was supposed to be Hime-senpai's stage.

00:12:58.420 --> 00:13:01.170
Hime-senpai and I are completely different.

00:13:02.170 --> 00:13:06.090
Even from the same stage, what we see before us is nothing alike.

00:13:07.180 --> 00:13:09.850
What now? I can't do this!

00:13:09.850 --> 00:13:11.720
I'll have to—{could also be "get them to pick someone else to do it", etc.}

00:13:11.100 --> 00:13:11.720
Yume.

00:13:13.140 --> 00:13:15.310
You made your decision to do this.

00:13:15.310 --> 00:13:16.940
Don't disappoint me.

00:13:17.730 --> 00:13:20.980
Wait! Rola!

00:13:33.080 --> 00:13:35.660
I never had a chance...

00:13:43.760 --> 00:13:45.800
Ow...

00:13:47.840 --> 00:13:49.260
Boiled octopus?

00:13:49.260 --> 00:13:52.010
I told you to stop calling me that!

00:13:55.890 --> 00:13:59.060
I see what's going on. So what now?

00:13:59.060 --> 00:14:01.020
How am I supposed to know?

00:14:01.820 --> 00:14:03.860
Just quit if you don't have the confidence.

00:14:03.860 --> 00:14:06.780
But it's too late for that...

00:14:06.780 --> 00:14:09.030
Then you'll just have to do it.

00:14:09.490 --> 00:14:10.660
But...

00:14:10.660 --> 00:14:13.120
So which? Pick one already.

00:14:14.200 --> 00:14:17.040
I don't know who I should be singing for.

00:14:18.460 --> 00:14:20.540
Ugh, fine.

00:14:20.540 --> 00:14:21.630
Come.

00:14:21.630 --> 00:14:23.300
Huh? Hey, wait!

00:14:23.300 --> 00:14:24.840
Where are we going?

00:14:24.840 --> 00:14:26.760
Just shut up and follow me.

00:14:28.180 --> 00:14:30.930
Nijino Yume's First Solo Live!

00:14:30.930 --> 00:14:32.810
We're selling tickets!

00:14:33.260 --> 00:14:34.010
Look.

00:14:34.010 --> 00:14:35.810
Would you like a ticket?

00:14:36.560 --> 00:14:38.060
It is going to be good? {Nico and Koko!}

00:14:38.060 --> 00:14:42.110
Of course! We can hardly wait ourselves.

00:14:42.110 --> 00:14:45.610
Yume-chan's going to put on an unforgettable performance!

00:14:45.610 --> 00:14:47.070
Those two...

00:14:47.070 --> 00:14:51.820
At the very least, those two are looking forward to it.

00:14:53.120 --> 00:14:53.830
And by the way,

00:14:54.280 --> 00:14:55.910
it was only one ticket for me.

00:14:57.080 --> 00:14:59.410
I sold just one ticket for my first live.{I wonder if this will be important}

00:14:59.410 --> 00:15:00.830
Just one?!

00:15:01.170 --> 00:15:03.500
It doesn't matter how many people show up.

00:15:03.500 --> 00:15:06.590
If you can satisfy the one fan before you,

00:15:06.590 --> 00:15:10.180
next it'll be ten, and then a hundred,

00:15:10.180 --> 00:15:12.550
and one day even over a thousand.

00:15:14.300 --> 00:15:16.600
I saw her taiyaki audition!

00:15:17.060 --> 00:15:19.230
She's holding a concert soon.{I remember some Japanese educational material offered "in the near future" as the translation of 今度 and me thinking that was silly, yet here I am}

00:15:19.230 --> 00:15:22.150
Yume-chan is? I wanna see!

00:15:22.150 --> 00:15:23.360
Let's go!

00:15:24.520 --> 00:15:26.860
Come on, you do have fans.

00:15:26.860 --> 00:15:28.360
Everyone...

00:15:29.530 --> 00:15:31.110
I won't give up.

00:15:31.490 --> 00:15:34.370
I'll never give up!

00:15:34.990 --> 00:15:36.030
Thank you!

00:15:43.710 --> 00:15:45.340
Sensei!

00:15:49.460 --> 00:15:51.760
Sensei, please train me!

00:15:51.760 --> 00:15:53.340
I need you!

00:15:54.890 --> 00:15:57.760
Okay. I won't go easy on you.

00:15:58.470 --> 00:16:00.770
One, two! One, two!

00:16:00.770 --> 00:16:02.850
You're off. One more time.

00:16:02.850 --> 00:16:03.730
Okay!

00:16:13.280 --> 00:16:16.740
Good, your movements are much sharper. Keep it up!

00:16:16.740 --> 00:16:17.780
Okay!

00:16:18.330 --> 00:16:21.160
Nijino-san is still at it this late. {it wasn't clear that way}

00:16:21.160 --> 00:16:25.790
Yume is trying to pull off the greatest performance she possibly can.

00:16:26.460 --> 00:16:31.050
If you were in her shoes, would you be able to stand firm against everything?

00:16:33.050 --> 00:16:37.680
One, two! One, two! One, two! One, two!

00:16:42.810 --> 00:16:44.310
Isn't this exciting, Koko? {yeah I guess this spelling is right, but that probably means we need to use Niko for the older one insetad of Nico}

00:16:44.310 --> 00:16:45.440
Yeah!

00:16:54.400 --> 00:16:55.070
Come in.

00:16:56.370 --> 00:16:57.320
Yume!

00:16:57.320 --> 00:16:59.790
Dad! Mom!

00:16:59.790 --> 00:17:01.910
Congratulations on getting your first live.

00:17:01.910 --> 00:17:03.410
Congrats.

00:17:03.410 --> 00:17:04.870
Thanks!

00:17:04.870 --> 00:17:06.380
Here, this is for you.

00:17:09.670 --> 00:17:13.470
It's a new creation we made while thinking of how you'd look on stage.

00:17:13.470 --> 00:17:14.930
Yume-chan!

00:17:15.970 --> 00:17:18.800
It's nice to see you both again. {I hate this}{or "Yume's Mom and Dad" or "Mr. and Mrs. Nijino" or "Aunt-san and Uncle-san" autc.}

00:17:18.800 --> 00:17:21.350
Koharu-chan, you're looking well.

00:17:21.350 --> 00:17:23.310
I am, thank you.

00:17:23.310 --> 00:17:26.060
Hello, my name is Sakuraba Rola.

00:17:26.060 --> 00:17:28.610
I'm friends with Yume.

00:17:28.610 --> 00:17:32.610
That's great. Please take care of her, Rola-chan.

00:17:32.610 --> 00:17:37.860
Right, I didn't see that many people in the lobby. Is everyone coming later?

00:17:37.860 --> 00:17:38.870
Nope.

00:17:38.870 --> 00:17:41.240
It doesn't matter how many people come.

00:17:41.240 --> 00:17:45.620
I'm still going to sing the best I can for those who came to see me.

00:17:46.460 --> 00:17:47.710
Nijino-san.

00:17:48.250 --> 00:17:50.920
Do you mind if we watch?

00:17:50.920 --> 00:17:54.760
We rushed to finish our work for Hime-senpai early.

00:17:56.510 --> 00:17:57.760
Of course!

00:18:05.640 --> 00:18:07.190
Made it!

00:18:12.730 --> 00:18:15.280
This is my start line.

00:18:15.780 --> 00:18:18.780
Nijino Yume, ready to go! {I actually looked for this line, but I think it's the first time}{it's like she's a strike witch ready for takeoff}

00:21:16.420 --> 00:21:18.750
I've never seen a concert like this before!{resist of temptation}

00:21:18.750 --> 00:21:20.800
Yeah, it's the best!

00:21:20.800 --> 00:21:23.130
Incredible, Yume-chan.

00:21:21.460 --> 00:21:23.130
Yume!

00:21:23.130 --> 00:21:24.930
She was totally different from usual.

00:21:23.130 --> 00:21:24.930
Yume-chan!

00:21:26.260 --> 00:21:28.180
It's the same as that time.

00:21:29.010 --> 00:21:30.510
Just like that performance...

00:21:36.600 --> 00:21:37.980
She's not half bad.{I think I remember D_S outchewing us for this in crimea edge}

00:21:41.360 --> 00:21:45.240
I see. Nijino Yume truly is...

00:21:55.000 --> 00:21:58.750
Everyone! Thank you!

00:22:00.920 --> 00:22:02.170
<i>Yume-chan!</i>

